  "__design__": [
    "The house has no warm ink, so the diverging ramp is dropped for a single-hue navy wash. Below-freezing stops being a colour state and becomes a number like any other.",
    "Every cell prints its value. Once the numbers are on the page the colour is doing ordering work only, and it is pushed back to a pale wash so the digits sit clearly on top.",
    "Key deleted. A gradient bar next to a grid of printed numbers restates what the numbers already say.",
    "Both axes stripped of domain, ticks and titles; city names left-aligned in navy, months in a lighter grey above the grid.",
    "Numbers reverse out to white on the four darkest steps and stay navy elsewhere — the switch is on the value, not on the row.",
    "Generous 26px cells with a 0.8px white gutter — the grid is spaced to be read as a table, which is what it now is."
  ],
